# Proposed Firestore rules change — review only

**Status:** proposal/diff only. This file is not a deployable replacement for `firestore.rules`. The authoritative `firestore.rules` file is intentionally untouched.

## Diff (conceptual)

```diff
 function actualDataAccessOpen(){
   return exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/systemSettings/actualDataAccess)
     && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/systemSettings/actualDataAccess).data.get("enabled",false)==true
     && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/systemSettings/actualDataAccess).data.get("status","")=="OPEN"
     && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/systemSettings/actualDataAccess).data.get("finalTestsAttested",false)==true;
 }
+// Proposed helper: a closed gate must not be bypassed by a malformed or
+// unrecognised origin marker. Keep the existing trial-origin compatibility
+// only for explicitly marked trial records.
+function validTrialOrigin(data){
+  return data.get("recordOrigin","") in ["TRIAL","trial","Trial"]
+    || data.get("trialData",false)==true
+    || data.get("isTrial",false)==true;
+}
 function actualCreateAllowed(){
-  return actualDataAccessOpen()||trialDataRecord(request.resource.data);
+  return actualDataAccessOpen()||validTrialOrigin(request.resource.data);
 }
 function actualUpdateAllowed(){
-  return actualDataAccessOpen()||(trialDataRecord(resource.data)&&trialDataRecord(request.resource.data));
+  return actualDataAccessOpen()
+    ||(validTrialOrigin(resource.data)&&validTrialOrigin(request.resource.data));
 }
 function actualDeleteAllowed(){
-  return actualDataAccessOpen()||trialDataRecord(resource.data);
+  return actualDataAccessOpen()||validTrialOrigin(resource.data);
 }
```

## Reasons and limitations

1. Makes the trial-origin exception explicit at the call site and documents that it is an exception to the closed-by-default actual-data gate.
2. Preserves the current accepted trial markers and existing access-gate behavior; it does not grant any new user role or collection access.
3. This refactor is behavior-equivalent to the current `trialDataRecord` helper, so it is documentation/clarity rather than a substantive security tightening. A real tightening requires a collection-by-collection rules review and emulator tests.
4. Do not deploy this proposal as-is. It is a review note, not a full rules file. Before adoption, produce a complete diff against the current rules and run the Firestore Rules Unit Testing suite. No production rules or data have been changed.
